FlatPatch: resolve-indexed-ancestors-without-rollout-scans

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Avoid repeated directory scans while resolving retained paginated fork history.

Requires: none

Provides: Use an existing SQLite path when its immutable rollout filename exactly matches the requested ancestor, including archived and compressed files; retain filesystem lookup for absent, stale or reverted selections.

Boundary: Preserve current-thread selection, immutable fork cutoffs, canonical managed-root reference validation, compression ownership, persistence acknowledgements and profile behavior; add no cache or index.

Verification: Lineage tests resolve indexed archived and compressed ancestors without listing unrelated sessions and preserve original immutable ancestry after index changes; the retained sixty-application profile reproduction measures end-to-end impact.


